# Normalize line endings to LF in the repository.
#
# Without this, Git on Windows rewrites checked-out files to CRLF, which produces
# a wall of warnings on every add and makes the working tree differ from the
# committed bytes. The source is authored and generated on Windows, so pinning LF
# keeps diffs clean and the generated artifacts (SVG, HTML) byte-stable.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary artifacts must never be text-normalized.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.parquet binary

# Generated output is line-ending sensitive only insofar as it is diffed; keep LF.
*.svg text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
